    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented customerCode collision de-duplication in `AssignCustomerCode.java` \u2014 the step in the `POST /api/owners` pipeline that assigns the code.\n\n**What changed** (`src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/AssignCustomerCode.java`):\n\n- Injected `OwnerRepository` into the `service` method (same by-type injection pattern used by the neighboring `AssignNamesakeCount` step).\n- After computing the base code `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, it now checks it against every existing owner's `customerCode`. If the base code is free, it's used as-is. On collision, it appends `-<n>` starting at `n=2` and increments to the smallest `n` that isn't already taken, then sets that de-duplicated code.\n\n**Why it's correct in this pipeline:**\n- `AssignCustomerCode` runs *before* `SaveOwner`, so the owner being created isn't yet persisted and can't collide with itself (mirrors the existing \"runs before save\" guarantee used by the namesake/duplicate steps).\n- Existing codes that already carry a `-<n>` suffix are collected into the taken-set too, so the loop never re-issues an occupied suffix.\n\n**Tests:** The full suite is green \u2014 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` and `BUILD SUCCESS`. The `AcceptanceTest.coreCustomerCodesStayUnique` test (which asserts distinct owners always get distinct customerCodes \u2014 the black-box observable guarantee of the rule) passes.",
